---
layout: layouts/page.njk
permalink: /phone/applications/mobile/android/
title: "VoiceTel Phone for Android — Install Guide"
description: "Install VoiceTel Phone or VoiceML Phone on Android from Google Play, allow microphone and notification access, and sign in to start calling."
---
{%- set voicetel = phoneApps.apps[0] %}

<p class="eyebrow"><a href="/phone/">VoiceTel Phone</a> &middot; <a href="/phone/applications/mobile/">Mobile</a> &middot; Android</p>
<h1>VoiceTel Phone for Android.</h1>
<p class="lede">Install from Google Play, sign in, and keep calls running in the background with a foreground-service notification that carries Mute and Hold controls. VoiceML Phone, the same softphone for VoiceML accounts, is on Google Play too.</p>
<p class="hero-actions">
	<a class="btn btn-primary" href="{{ voicetel.stores.android }}">Get it on Google Play</a>
	<a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/phone/applications/mobile/">All mobile clients</a>
</p>

<section id="install" class="section-block">
	<h2>1. Install from Google Play</h2>
	<div class="oss-cards">
		{%- for app in phoneApps.apps %}
		<article class="oss-card">
			<header class="oss-card__header">
				<span class="oss-card__icon">{% icon "phone-vibrate" %}</span>
				<h3 class="oss-card__title">{{ app.name }}</h3>
			</header>
			<p class="oss-card__description">{{ app.audience }}</p>
			<p class="oss-card__url"><a href="{{ app.stores.android }}">{{ app.name }} on Google Play</a></p>
		</article>
		{%- endfor %}
	</div>
</section>

<section id="firstlaunch" class="section-block">
	<h2>2. First launch</h2>
	<ol>
		<li>Allow <strong>microphone</strong> access when prompted; calls need it.</li>
		<li>Allow <strong>notifications</strong> so incoming calls reach you while the app is in the background or closed.</li>
		<li>Optionally allow <strong>contacts</strong> access to dial from your address book.</li>
		<li>Sign in. VoiceTel Phone takes the SIP credentials provisioned in the VoiceTel customer portal; VoiceML Phone takes a VoiceML activation code under <em>Settings &rarr; Auto Provision</em>.</li>
	</ol>
</section>

<section id="faq" class="section-block faq-block">
	<h2>FAQ</h2>
	<details class="faq-item">
		<summary>Which app do I need?</summary>
		<p>VoiceTel Phone for VoiceTel accounts; VoiceML Phone for VoiceML accounts. Both are free on Google Play.</p>
	</details>
	<details class="faq-item">
		<summary>Incoming calls don't ring when the app is in the background</summary>
		<p>Make sure notifications are allowed for the app, and exclude it from battery optimization (<em>Settings &rarr; Apps &rarr;</em> the app &rarr; <em>Battery</em> &rarr; <em>Unrestricted</em>) so Android doesn't stop it in the background.</p>
	</details>
	<details class="faq-item">
		<summary>The other person can't hear me</summary>
		<p>Open <em>Settings &rarr; Apps &rarr;</em> the app &rarr; <em>Permissions</em> and allow <em>Microphone</em>.</p>
	</details>
</section>

<aside class="cta-block" aria-labelledby="phone-android-cta-heading">
	<h2 id="phone-android-cta-heading">Need credentials first?</h2>
	<p>Sign up to provision SIP credentials, then install VoiceTel Phone on every Android device that needs to make calls.</p>
	<p class="hero-actions">
		<a class="btn btn-primary" href="/signup/">Sign up</a>
		<a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/phone/applications/mobile/">All mobile clients</a>
	</p>
</aside>
